eeper into the data at this  relationship  and why is that happening that was  entirely sure you know it might be  might it be because the viral load is  lower at the moment so people aren't  getting as much of the disease  might it be that we are getting better  at treating the disease certainly  there's some evidence for that that  people are surviving more in intensive  care  when they come down with this disease so  some encouraging news there  but in practice no one really knows it's  one of the things about covert 19  so many mysteries which is why you know  we just keep looking at the data and  keep  not fixing upon one answer and remaining  relatively open to new explanations as  they come along  and while there are no flashing red  lights clearly uh it's important to be  vigilant about this  vigilance about the rising cases  vigilance it's certainly about the rise  uh in deaths if that does indeed happen  uh and vigilant two about  series like this this shows the number  of people in hospitals  and right now again no flashing red  lights  uh there is not an increase really  there's a slight increase in the last  few days but  nothing like a trend you know more like  noise uh in admissions to  hospital for covert 19 and we need to  keep an eye to  on tests and the number of cases that  are coming back positive because it does  look like it's going up and here's where  the  which the one thing i'm really quite  concerned about over the course of the  past few days it's not just those  overall numbers  it is the fact that there are signs that  the testing system which we were told  was now  you know world class is creaking  uh right now there have been anecdotal  stories i've heard from a few people  in the last few days about them trying  to get a test and not being able to do  so  that's pretty worrying given that we are  seeing cases rising and people are going  to be concerned about  that and you can't get the economy going  again and  have the disease bei